# Line endings, so a Windows checkout still builds and runs the container.
#
# Git for Windows converts text files to CRLF on checkout by default
# (core.autocrlf=true). That is harmless for Python, Markdown and JSON, and
# fatal for what a POSIX shell or the Linux container executes: with CRLF,
# docker/entrypoint.sh fails with "set: Illegal option -" and the container
# with "exec /usr/local/bin/entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory".
# These rules hold whatever core.autocrlf the person cloning has set.

# Let Git decide text vs binary; the repository itself stores LF.
* text=auto

# Executed by sh, make or docker: always LF, on every platform.
*.sh       text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile   text eol=lf
